{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791105602383,"sessionID":"ses_ef9c9eeffffe1x7vpuKVbHZY1q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"rehearsal_submit_answer","callID":"tool_Wyxq4wDYfKi6oKKgR3xzEOPh","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"answer":{"findings":[{"gap":"The requirement mandates a flat grammar where the alternate word ends at the first closing brace and is never recursively interpolated, but the grader's 'literal' case only checks a brace-free word ($OTHER, empty, α/β) and a malformed unterminated expression; it never puts a closing brace inside the word. Therefore a repair that adds nested-brace matching/expansion for ${...} inside the word (while still leaving bare $OTHER literal) passes every grader case yet violates the flat-grammar rule.","wrong_repair":"A repair that balances nested braces so that in ${BASE:+${OTHER}} the word is ${OTHER} and is recursively expanded.","input":"os.environ.update(BASE='yes', OTHER='expanded'); dotenv_values(stream=io.StringIO('OUT=${BASE:+${OTHER}}\\n'))","expected":"Per the requirement ('word ends at the first closing brace and is not recursively interpolated'), OUT == '${OTHER}' (literal word '${OTHER' plus the trailing '}'). The nested-expansion repair yields 'expanded' and is still accepted by the grader.","citations":[{"source":"src1:641f7e98e8b766d36418d7966fc3f6b12f36ab6c991d245344f49c5ac93c2b8d"},{"source":"src1:da62f9a2d934ed6c620923aad478f1d19561b73de5afaf670aec99f96771ff36"}]}],"limitations":"Reviewed only the flat/nonrecursive and literal-word aspect against the supplied packet; the full grader beyond byte 4413 and other parser files were not inspected, so other acceptance gaps may exist."}},"output":"{\"submitted\":true}","metadata":{"truncated":false},"title":"","time":{"start":1791105602365,"end":1791105602373}},"id":"prt_106367853001QDr0NTTFUtBH9j","sessionID":"ses_ef9c9eeffffe1x7vpuKVbHZY1q","messageID":"msg_1063614dc001AHQ4DwMTY17Qgl"}}
